  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Performance Management and Evaluation Services (PMES)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Iraq):  Risks associated with the current security situation and the fluid political environment in Iraq severely limit the mobility of USAID&apos;s expatriate and local staff, and the ability of implementing partner expatriate staff from carrying out regular monitoring and evaluation activities.The Performance Management and Evaluation Services (PMES) activity will enable the USAID Mission to improve and adapt its performance management needs to fulfill its monitoring, evaluation, reporting, and information-sharing obligations as mandated in USAID&apos;s Automated Directives System (ADS) and other agency guidance. PMES will also enable USAID to 1) ensure implementing partners&apos; compliance with USAID&apos;s policies and regulations, including developing and maintaining a Performance Management Plan (PMP), and Data Quality Assessments (DQAs), 2) survey, analyze, and evaluate service performance, 3) build capacity for USAID and implementing partners staff on monitoring, evaluation, and learning, and 4) support the Mission to advance its collaboration, learning, and adaptation efforts.</narrative>
  </description>
